t","uuid":"d0daf358-bc52-406b-95cb-325fe2eff41b","session_id":"824540e8-f13e-4561-93d4-f3f912d801e1","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"d0daf358-bc52-406b-95cb-325fe2eff41b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"deepseek-chat","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_wn1cjtCtTu0JUsllF3TP5320","name":"write_file","input":{"file_path":"/home/runner/.qwen/memories/feedback/write-file-regex-escaping.md","content":"---\nname: Qwen tool Write file escapes backslashes in regex literals\ndescription: The write_file tool emits `\\\\s` instead of `\\s` inside JS regex literals, which breaks them at parse time; verify regexes after writing regex-heavy files\ntype: feedback\ncategory: common_pitfall\nkeywords:\n  - \"write_file regex backslash escaping\"\n  - \"tool artifact invalid regular expression\"\n  - \"js regex literal double backslash\"\nusage_scenarios:\n  - \"Writing JS/TS files that contain regex literals\"\n  - \"Debugging SyntaxError Invalid regular expression after a file write\"\n---\n\nThe `write_file` tool can turn `\\s`/`\\b` inside a JavaScript regex literal into a literal `\\\\s`, producing\n`SyntaxError: Invalid regular expression: Nothing to repeat` when the module is loaded.\n\n**Why:** observed twice-ish in this repo (portal/read-with-you/tts.js) — the written file differed from the intended content.\n\n**How to apply:** after writing a regex-heavy file, run it once (node --test / node -e import) before building on top of it; if it fails to parse, re-check the regex source and fix with the `edit` tool rather than rewriting the whole file.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_01_1YNCNpy5Dq0oZ6x2WqOz5715","name":"write_file","input":{"file_path":"/home/runner/.qwen/projects/-home-runner-work-zero-one-workbench-zero-one-workbench/memory/project/c01-rebuild-under-read-with-you.md","content":"---\nname: Reader repo ignores its own product surfaces when judging C01\ndescription: Existing C01 reader (portal/reader-integrated.*) has weak whole-book reading (no pagination/percentage, clientSpeechSynthesis-only TTS) despite docs claiming foliate integration; D博士 authorized a rebuild under portal/read-with-you/\ntype: project\ncategory: important_decision\nkeywords:\n  - \"read with you C01 rebuild\"\n  - \"portal/read-with-you\"\n  - \"folio narration independent reader\"\nusage_scenarios:\n  - \"Continuing Read With You product work\"\n  - \"Comparing old reader-integrated implementation with new reader\"\n---\n\nAs of 2026-10-24 (issue #42 latest authorization), D博士 is the sole product owner of 「陪你读书」 and may rebuild C01.\nThe pre-existing `portal/reader-integrated.html/.js` (foliate-js + browser SpeechSynthesis) is retained as evidence,\nnot as the product; the new product lives at `portal/read-with-you/` (index.html, reader.html, state.js, tts.js, voice-lab.js, library-ui.js).\n\n**Why:** the user's unabridged vision (whole-book reading, continuous cross-chapter narration with resume, notes,\nbackground audio, authorized family voice, listening world) exceeds what the old integrated page did; C博士's old\n\"must keep / must deliver\" protocol no longer binds D博士.\n\n**How to apply:** continue product work under `portal/read-with-you/`; do not treat legacy docs (docs/c01/CORE-DEVELOPMENT.md)\nor old acceptance gates as requirements, and do not spend cycles on the legacy page except as a link target.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":76608,"output_tokens":778,"cache_read_input_tokens":76032,"total_tokens":77386}}},{"type":"user","uuid":"2c3da761-b2a7-4a8f-bee8-20aa110bc0d1","session_id":"824540e8-f13e-4561-93d4-f3f912d801e1","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_wn1cjtCtTu0JUsllF3TP5320","is_error":false,"content":"Successfully overwrote file: /home/runner/.qwen/memories/feedback/write-file-regex-escaping.md."}]}},{"type":"user","uuid":"66d5ac0d-260a-4664-9269-1c5fdd6539ce","session_id":"824540e8-f13e-4561-93d4-f3f912d8