d.\n3. 听世界 is links to the existing radio/watch pages plus two curated live streams; there is no general podcast directory or host-transcript/translation pipeline yet.\n4. The 读伴 discussion panel is deliberately local and deterministic (quote + questions + notes); no cloud or local LLM is wired in.\n5. I could not verify anything in a browser this turn — the e2e suite does not exist yet, so nothing beyond the 14 unit tests is proven.\n\nBefore this can merge, `reader.js` must be finished (overlayer highlight, chapter-walk generator, panels, settings, voice lab wiring), `index.html`/`library-ui.js` built, fixtures + Playwright e2e written, and `portal/index.html` linked to the new reader."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":87415,"output_tokens":648,"cache_read_input_tokens":86400,"total_tokens":88063}}},{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"c855049e-a1d1-4955-9e79-b858014c5cf3","session_id":"824540e8-f13e-4561-93d4-f3f912d801e1","is_error":false,"duration_ms":460899,"duration_api_ms":435432,"num_turns":108,"result":"I've stopped chasing the memory index; the two memory files are written and readable, so I'm moving on to the actual product work.\n\nCurrent status of the rebuild under `portal/read-with-you/`:\n\n**Done and syntax-checked**\n- `state.js` — IndexedDB library store, positions, bookmarks, notes, settings, voices, privacy audit, legacy migration, export/import, cascade delete\n- `tts.js` — sentence splitter, plain-text chapter parser, SSML→sentence segments, `Narration` engine over an injectable speech engine (14 unit tests pass)\n- `app.css`, `reader.css` — paper shelf + reading room styling, night/sepia themes, focus mode\n- `ui.js`, `notes.js` (读伴 helpers: excerpt, prompts, gentle lines, highlight terms), `family-voice.js` (consent → enroll → profile → revoke → purge, no cloning), `ambience.js` (generated loop WAVs), `background.js` (ducking background audio + curated radio), `reader.html`, `package.json`\n\n**Incomplete, as I'm handing